    },
    {
      "before": "This manuscript, its code and its certificates were produced by Claude Fable 5.1 agents (Anthropic) working under the author's direction, in three roles: two author agents (working report of 2026-09-12/13, the second resuming the first after a usage limit; no fallback to another model occurred), an independent adversarial review agent (review of 2026-09-13), whose findings are incorporated with attribution in Sections 2, 5 and 7, and a writing agent (this text, the three manuscript scripts and the rerun of 2026-09-13). The certificates are exact rational objects checked by two independently written verifiers; the mathematical content of the theorems rests on them and on the four imported results listed in Section 3. No human peer review has taken place. Scientific responsibility rests with the author.",
      "after": "The author supplied the original manuscript, code and certificates as work produced with Claude Fable 5.1, with authoring, adversarial-review and writing roles described in the delivery. These are author-supplied historical identities and role descriptions; neither the serving configuration nor isolation of those sessions has been authenticated here. On 14 September 2026, native Codex reviews configured as GPT-6 Astra High and GPT-5.6 Sol Medium assessed the original exact PDF in fresh delegated tasks and ran separate exact checks. The coordinator then prepared this corrected candidate, including the componentwise dual condition in Section 4.3 and reporting corrections. Those original-PDF assessments are preserved separately and do not constitute assessments or acceptance of this new PDF. No independent human peer review is claimed. The mathematical content rests on the exact certificates and the imported results listed in Section 3. Scientific responsibility rests with the author."
    },
    {
      "before": "## 8. Observations and open questions",
      "after": "**Fresh checks of 14 September 2026.** The coordinator replayed the supplied full verifier in a separate work copy: all certificates passed, with `TOTAL: 0 failures`, in 268.969 seconds. A fresh Astra High task independently reconstructed the finite pair sets, Horn membership using Littlewood–Richardson tableaux, and chamber rays using integer cofactors, without importing the submitted Python code: 47,685 vertex primals, 20 minimiser duals, 34 additional primal-dual entries, 12 active all-d files, 522 dimension-six Horn triples and all 112 chamber-ray incidences passed. A fresh Sol Medium task separately checked the dimension-six chamber certificates and all-d inequalities. Both reviews concerned the original PDF; the underlying certificate bytes and verifier code are unchanged in this corrected candidate. Section 4.3 now states the componentwise coefficient bound actually satisfied by all stored duals (equality is unnecessary). These checks are computational evidence, not human peer review or a proof of model-session independence. Historical scripts and logs remain preserved as historical evidence.\n\n## 8. Observations and open questions"
    }
